            <ArticleTitle>Reviewing the causes of electrocardiographic pauses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-260</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5830/CVJA-2017-041</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The electrocardiographic term 'pause' refers to the prolonged R-R interval that represents the interruption in ventricular depolarisation. This article presents a case of sinus node dysfunction and provides a diagnostic approach to pauses on the ECG.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
